bulance). Keep your hotel card with address in Japanese so taxis can find it.\n\n10) Quick checklist before you go out each day\n   - Suica has enough balance (top up if low).  \n   - Phone charged, portable battery if needed.  \n   - Hotel card (Japanese address) or saved location in maps.  \n   - Small cash for places that don\u2019t take cards.  \n   - Confirm return train times if you\u2019re going far from the city center.\n\nIf you want, I can:\n- Put together step-by-step directions (with transfer details and times) for any specific trip you\u2019re planning in Tokyo; or  \n- Help you prepare a printable (or phone-ready) cheat sheet with station names, transfer lines, and Japanese addresses for your hotel and main sights. Which would be most helpful?", "autoeval_label": {"model": "gpt-4o-2024-08-06", "label": true}}
